# A correct transcript for the dry run. The runner fills in each
# {{edit_tag PATH}} with the tag that workspace_read_lines gives for the file
# as it is at that moment, as a model copies it from the read result.
# The first edit of src/a.rs comes after the read of src/b.rs. When the
# harness keeps only the latest read, that edit is refused and the agent
# reads src/a.rs again; when it keeps both, the second edit of src/a.rs
# writes the same line again. Both ways end with both files changed.
>>> call workspace_read_lines
{"path":"src/a.rs","start_line":1,"end_line":2}
>>> call workspace_read_lines
{"path":"src/b.rs","start_line":1,"end_line":2}
>>> call workspace_edit_lines
{"path":"src/a.rs","start_line":2,"end_line":2,"edit_tag":"{{edit_tag src/a.rs}}","operation":"replace","new_text":"pub const SCHEMA_A: u32 = 4;\n"}
>>> call workspace_read_lines
{"path":"src/a.rs","start_line":1,"end_line":2}
>>> call workspace_edit_lines
{"path":"src/a.rs","start_line":2,"end_line":2,"edit_tag":"{{edit_tag src/a.rs}}","operation":"replace","new_text":"pub const SCHEMA_A: u32 = 4;\n"}
>>> call workspace_read_lines
{"path":"src/b.rs","start_line":1,"end_line":2}
>>> call workspace_edit_lines
{"path":"src/b.rs","start_line":2,"end_line":2,"edit_tag":"{{edit_tag src/b.rs}}","operation":"replace","new_text":"pub const SCHEMA_B: u32 = 4;\n"}
>>> answer
`SCHEMA_A` and `SCHEMA_B` are now 4.
